{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-9de07d6caefe8fb780ca602b10ae992ffa91044f2c10921e","family_id":"KR:007467","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Rules on Measurement of Ship Tonnage","title_original":"선박톤수의 측정에 관한 규칙","kind":"해양수산부령","source_version":"233591","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=233591","source_sha256":"86d0a65be806f7367d84c8e503c399209a614e2ef6ffb877cf8a6bbdcaf5f140","body_sha256":"931878fc8fb77897481d211849fb4979fc238c900b48d586ad10c6aecfda1428","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 36 (Calculation of Gross Tonnage of Ships Having Two or More Decks)\n(1) The gross tonnage of a ship having two or more decks shall be the value obtained by multiplying the international gross tonnage under Article 9 by the coefficient calculated by the following formula, expressed in measurement tons:\n\n(0.6 + t/10,000) × (1 + (30 − t)/180) · (B/A − 0.25)\n\nt: International gross tonnage under Article 9.\nA: Moulded depth at the midpoint of the length between perpendiculars less the value prescribed in Appendix 6 according to the applicable category of length between perpendiculars (hereinafter the same applies in this Article).\nB: Vertical distance, at the midpoint of the length between perpendiculars, from the lower end of the moulded depth to the underside of the second deck at the ship's side (hereinafter the same applies in this Article).\n\nWhere the value of (0.6 + t/10,000) is 1 or greater, that value shall be taken as 1.\nWhere the value of (1 + (30 − t)/180) is less than 1, that value shall be taken as 1.\nWhere the value of B/A is less than 0.7, that value shall be taken as 0.7.\n\n(2) A ship whose gross tonnage is calculated under paragraph (1) shall be a ship marking a load line under Article 27 of the Ship Safety Act and shall meet the following requirements: <Amended on November 23, 2007>\n1. The load line shall be at or below the lower end of the freeboard calculated under the Load Line Regulations with the second deck counted from the upper deck (hereinafter referred to as the \"second deck\") treated as the freeboard deck.\n2. The spaces between the forward and after bulkheads between the upper deck and the second deck shall be machinery spaces, cargo spaces (excluding spaces for carrying unpackaged liquids or gases), ship's stores, workshops or spaces ancillary to those spaces.\n3. The following formula shall be satisfied:\n\nB/A ≤ 0.9\n\n[Source graphic annotation: In the last formula, the frozen XML renders the comparison sign as a question mark. The held original image, flSeq 8412136, was actually inspected and shows B/A less than or equal to 0.9. The verified inequality is displayed above; the original XML and image evidence are preserved unchanged.]\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_title_record":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1522_KR000068\\translations\\tonnage_rule\\en.title.json","sha256":"c897b8af8593e31fdc2f6cb0caef7bbf94c13d2953aacc9e1b32bc312a7cd2e9"},"author_unit_artifacts":[{"json":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1522_KR000068\\translations\\tonnage_rule\\en.units.parts\\article-36.json","sha256":"f973026e63a9a360e69e863b0890fea32f500da56d8034a9bb772fd4c7f665f9"},"selfcheck":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1522_KR000068\\translations\\tonnage_rule\\en.units.parts\\article-36.selfcheck.json","sha256":"5143203aade656a994c049cf9c443b116745d651ddd7446953fcb81f84a22493"},"text":{"path":"D:\\lawsof